          }
        ],
        "text": "This theory suggests that when our attention is divided, we take in environmental information subconsciously, so that when we return to full awareness and pay attention, we feel we have seen it all before.",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n4. **The Pattern/Similarity Theory:** ",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          {
            "cited_text": "The similarity between a d\u00e9j\u00e0-vu\u2013eliciting stimulus and an existing, or non-existing but different, memory trace may lead to the sensation that an eve...",
            "encrypted_index": "EpEBCioIEBgCIiRkMmJjZWZjOS0wNDQwLTQxYWUtOTM0Mi1hNDFhNjdkYWIzZWQSDKab5hmVwq4iE+nvvBoMz80ITYkGPk3+QBHmIjCYU9WMEdPMVorklznaPLyO59IUjOqEPwCfjRJRI90Pz/c5l/A8Hwf0wfess800jvkqFVILoG2uLwBhc8akZ6wyMehC/r8JnBgE",
